      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c894acb14c12bfd94265cc44df4307c2cf6abcd512db69f2d7abebe5e0197283",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Embedding ξ in the heat-deformed family H_t turns RH into the zero geometry of the t=0 slice and the de Bruijn–Newman theorem turns persistence of real zeros into a threshold Λ. For the selected close pair, the Lehmer gap-versus-background certificate and its λ_K theorem then convert static zero geometry into the quantitative obstruction −5.895·10^-9<Λ.",
